, 							{
								"box" : 								{
									"id" : "obj-52",
									"linecount" : 15,
									"maxclass" : "comment",
									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 870.0, 0.0, 365.0, 179.0 ],
									"text" : "Order of operations:\n*. Song-specific (rather than instrument-specific) attributes – scale, total and current. Total can always be assessed ad hoc and current will always be set in the following steps. Current updates scale directly.\n2. UI elements recall – assesses total (after the read but before the recall) and sets current to total +1 then stores and sends sounds at new current (don't want to overwrite anything if song is already playing). This means an instrument loaded when a song is already playing will give you last-used not stored current sound\n3. Settings loaded – assesses total and if it's still 0 (should only happen the very first time the instrument is loaded) sets current to 1 then chooses_new_sound\n4. Song starts – after sounds dictionary loads set_current_to. If there is no current for this instrument, set it to a default of 1\n5. exporting 0 – clear sounds dictionary then reassert_in-use_sound (scale returns to default)"
								}

							}
